[[:db/retract 17592186344913 :answer-field/choices 17592186343346] [:db/retract 17592186344913 :answer-field/choices 17592186343657] [:db/retract 17592186344913 :answer-field/choices 17592186343818] [:db/retract 17592186344913 :answer-field/choices 17592186343865] [:db/retract 17592186344913 :answer-field/choices 17592186344159] {:db/id 17592186119818 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-64b2528a-be45-5f89-bf42-907c121c9d08" "question-4bcb849a-6acb-581b-82ad-febe08cc464f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-64b2528a-be45-5f89-bf42-907c121c9d08" :question/id #uuid "64b2528a-be45-5f89-bf42-907c121c9d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-74999" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e52557d-0afb-5f71-8fd0-5b680e7b62a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e52557d-0afb-5f71-8fd0-5b680e7b62a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e52557d-0afb-5f71-8fd0-5b680e7b62a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89907820-6a08-564d-b8ae-b65ce2c3fedd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72404e91-0b79-5fbe-bf3b-a415c48e7a6a" "answer-92e4bcf7-630e-5d3c-a886-783b15806935" "answer-3634eb4a-2da6-506c-862a-4df1259f8573" "answer-89907820-6a08-564d-b8ae-b65ce2c3fedd" "answer-a713ed5b-5694-581a-b057-41bc0b0505a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72404e91-0b79-5fbe-bf3b-a415c48e7a6a" :answer/id #uuid "72404e91-0b79-5fbe-bf3b-a415c48e7a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92e4bcf7-630e-5d3c-a886-783b15806935" :answer/id #uuid "92e4bcf7-630e-5d3c-a886-783b15806935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3634eb4a-2da6-506c-862a-4df1259f8573" :answer/id #uuid "3634eb4a-2da6-506c-862a-4df1259f8573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89907820-6a08-564d-b8ae-b65ce2c3fedd" :answer/id #uuid "89907820-6a08-564d-b8ae-b65ce2c3fedd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a713ed5b-5694-581a-b057-41bc0b0505a8" :answer/id #uuid "a713ed5b-5694-581a-b057-41bc0b0505a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{\\,\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345022 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{2}=-5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ -5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344913 :answer-field/correct "answer-fbc395a0-e334-5fc2-b91b-ac21c50346f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9846224a-bf7a-5c09-b38f-8a30ce03496d" "answer-11fe67bf-961a-57c3-a494-79893e59e352" "answer-fbc395a0-e334-5fc2-b91b-ac21c50346f9" "answer-d816478a-9661-5854-a6c9-b2d73c0f3b30" "answer-038d8f66-0fdf-5eca-b0da-b68e8724c6db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9846224a-bf7a-5c09-b38f-8a30ce03496d" :answer/id #uuid "9846224a-bf7a-5c09-b38f-8a30ce03496d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11fe67bf-961a-57c3-a494-79893e59e352" :answer/id #uuid "11fe67bf-961a-57c3-a494-79893e59e352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbc395a0-e334-5fc2-b91b-ac21c50346f9" :answer/id #uuid "fbc395a0-e334-5fc2-b91b-ac21c50346f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d816478a-9661-5854-a6c9-b2d73c0f3b30" :answer/id #uuid "d816478a-9661-5854-a6c9-b2d73c0f3b30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-038d8f66-0fdf-5eca-b0da-b68e8724c6db" :answer/id #uuid "038d8f66-0fdf-5eca-b0da-b68e8724c6db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{\\,\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bcb849a-6acb-581b-82ad-febe08cc464f" :question/id #uuid "4bcb849a-6acb-581b-82ad-febe08cc464f" :question/math-academy-id "q-111399" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{4}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=8{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{4}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1876c4ef-5464-51fa-81fc-f9807976cbf4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1876c4ef-5464-51fa-81fc-f9807976cbf4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1876c4ef-5464-51fa-81fc-f9807976cbf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3bfcd48e-1e57-5c21-853e-08ad7ac4a5f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-664c9ed3-862f-5378-872f-f842ae26bbab" "answer-95fafc91-7cf2-5717-8af6-6f0822454343" "answer-3bfcd48e-1e57-5c21-853e-08ad7ac4a5f7" "answer-df170ecc-0149-5c63-b255-b0c96ff08d83" "answer-d6697aa2-fa9e-539f-96c0-14b882489af7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-664c9ed3-862f-5378-872f-f842ae26bbab" :answer/id #uuid "664c9ed3-862f-5378-872f-f842ae26bbab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95fafc91-7cf2-5717-8af6-6f0822454343" :answer/id #uuid "95fafc91-7cf2-5717-8af6-6f0822454343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \